1
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,037
Evens wins!

2
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:06,950
Evens wins!

3
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:11,150
Evens wins!

4
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,050
Ooh!

5
00:00:15,133 --> 00:00:17,566
Looks like Lady Luck's
taking a liking to you!

6
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:18,860
Ain't that sweet?

7
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:22,020
You're really something else!

8
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:24,877
Not everyone can hit a
winning streak that grand!

9
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:25,790
For you.

10
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:32,037
That's for the sushi,
thanks for covering me.

11
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:35,797
Oh, I think you ended me a
bit too much there, chief.

12
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:38,580
I'll win some more, don't you worry.

13
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,010
Man,

14
00:00:42,093 --> 00:00:44,337
to think we were just
looking for shelter from the

15
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:47,937
rain—I got a good feeling
if I stick to your side;

16
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:49,437
I'll never go hungry, mister.

17
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:52,517
You might be the finest man in water.

18
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,430
water

19
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:59,340
Ugh, sake is going to taste
extra special tonight.

20
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:02,220
Place your bets.

21
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,240
Odds. Wow!

22
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:10,717
You said that was such
a beam of confidence.

23
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,880
Gave me chills.

24
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,680
Anyone else?

25
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:27,300
Last call, then.

26
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:33,420
Calling it!

27
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:40,160
It's odds!

28
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,111
Thought you had that one.

29
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:49,320
No sword style.

30
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:51,480
Tatsumaki!

31
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:11,140
Oh, looks like we caught a rat!

32
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:14,040
You guys are so Uncle.

33
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:20,120
Get the sky! Hurry up!

34
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:24,310
Hm.

35
00:02:24,393 --> 00:02:26,060
Free punching bags as well?

36
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,769
This place has everything.

37
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,860
Don't hold back. Take him down!

38
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,240
One Sword Style.

39
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,040
Great Dragon Shock!

40
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:18,920
Whoa, one sec, mister, I'm a firm
believer in good old balance.

41
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:22,017
Good and evil, black and
white, odds and evens.

42
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:25,020
You really got them good,
so let's call it a day.

43
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:26,410
Yeah.

44
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:30,459
I have a complaint for the manager.

45
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:34,116
And if I'm not mistaken,
that would be you, is it not?

46
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:37,600
Here, take it!

47
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:40,721
Just get the hell out of
here and don't come back!

48
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:48,797
One dream, one wish.

49
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:52,420
If you want it, gotta go over the top.

50
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:13,020
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

51
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:17,600
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

52
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:20,637
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no?

53
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:23,037
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

54
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:25,597
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

55
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:28,360
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

56
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:35,617
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

57
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:40,620
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

58
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:43,777
Despite all that to run is not an option.

59
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:45,897
Once they're close to
feel the satisfaction.

60
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:48,157
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

61
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:51,200
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

62
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:56,537
If you are going on your way.

63
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:58,777
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

64
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:01,937
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

65
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,460
Yes, I can.

66
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:06,277
As you're on your way.

67
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,537
Marked maps will be made.

68
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:11,500
Yes, with every step that you will take.

69
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,617
Just look at all you've been through.

70
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,857
Look ahead on new horizons in view.

71
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:21,040
Shining brightly, oh, who
knows what's waiting for you?

72
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:24,337
Dream living, that's the way.

73
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:26,377
Make like a hurricane.

74
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:29,340
Now, got to make your mark today.

75
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:35,377
One dream, one wish.

76
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,217
Your dreams don't run away.

77
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:40,197
Go for the knockout!

78
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:42,120
Over the top!

79
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:48,800
Man, oh man, I was shaking
like a leaf. What about you?

80
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:50,627
Could you shut up for a sec?

81
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:54,517
Why, that's a mighty kind suggestion,
my friend, and very perceptive.

82
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:58,377
Seeing as I've been running my mouth so
much, my throat could do with a bit of rest.

83
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:02,397
But more importantly, I realize I
haven't properly introduced myself.

84
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:05,997
The name's Turner Yasuie, but
everyone calls me Seek-a-Fit Yasuie.

85
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,080
Nice to meet you.

86
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,430
Wow.

87
00:06:09,513 --> 00:06:11,817
Even when you don't speak,
your mug says it all.

88
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,437
What a hunk, what a stud.

89
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:16,167
Why, I bet you can't
keep the ladies off you.

90
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:18,560
Why are you following me?

91
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:22,597
I got this really strong feeling
while we were at the gambling house.

92
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:26,737
That if I stepped by your side, then the
world would be all sunshine and rainbows.

93
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:28,417
I should have measured this back there.

94
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:30,377
But not everyone stands up for those guys.

95
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:32,357
They're underlings of the Kyoshiro family.

96
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:35,437
Ayaka's a group from the
capital, real dreadful lowlifes.

97
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:36,520
Know what I mean?

98
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:38,040
Man, I'm telling you.

99
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:41,985
If I were a woman, your heroics
would have me weak in the knees.

100
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,962
You see something ahead, mister?

101
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:48,840
I think I recognize that place. Woo-hoo!

102
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,280
I'm sure you do.

103
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:52,057
That'd be the flower capital.

104
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:53,477
And that settlement in front of it?

105
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:58,480
None other than Okobore, or more officially
Ebisu, which is also my hometown.

106
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,391
Your home sounds wealthy.

107
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:02,542
Ebisu's the god of good fortune.

108
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:04,660
There's a reason it has that name.

109
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,976
But you'll just have to wait and see.

110
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,637
All right.

111
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:11,550
Who's next?

112
00:07:11,633 --> 00:07:14,940
I'll take one bowl of Sabo. But of course.

113
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:17,500
That guy, who is he?

114
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:20,600
Beats me, but he sure draws a crowd.

115
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,000
Arrogant little playboy.

116
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:27,160
He has no clue whose
turf he's muscled it on.

117
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:29,480
That's all right.

118
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,260
We'll teach him.

119
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:39,780
Beat that iron!

120
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:47,820
Hold that stone!

121
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:01,120
It's fine if you can't work,

122
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:05,760
but at least have the decency
to die and get out of the way!

123
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:29,540
This is all?

124
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:31,740
I told you the rules.

125
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:34,720
All five blocks get one millet dumpling.

126
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:38,620
Is old man yo too frail to
earn his own food anymore?

127
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:40,057
What a shame.

128
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:42,117
you've stuck around long

129
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:47,297
enough time to kick the bucket I

130
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:50,637
worked so hard all day long huh

131
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:57,497
you got something to say the next

132
00:08:57,580 --> 00:09:01,337
time you talk back to a guard
I'll take one of your limbs off

133
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:08,180
next don't fight back you gotta
save your energy you old man, yo,

134
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:10,344
or you're going to end up dead.

135
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:12,990
Wow.

136
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,900
Four exchange tickets, huh?

137
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:16,892
Someone's a hard worker.

138
00:09:28,140 --> 00:09:29,560
Here I come.

139
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,657
Move it, you damn morons.

140
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:38,020
I'll run you over!

141
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:39,340
What's it, Jaggy?

142
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:40,480
I'm right here!

143
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:43,460
Then how about I run you over, too?

144
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:47,170
No!

145
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:11,740
Whoa, hold on. We're full.

146
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:14,019
You've brought us enough for today.

147
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:16,690
Full!

148
00:10:16,773 --> 00:10:18,417
Then you should bring another ship!

149
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:19,860
Quit slacking off!

150
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:22,100
Sorry, sir!

151
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:29,260
So, how many stones did those two haul?

152
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:31,780
I lost count at 500 or so.

153
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,270
Huh?

154
00:10:33,353 --> 00:10:34,183
Then they're handcuffs?

155
00:10:34,266 --> 00:10:35,096
Sea prism stones.

156
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:39,580
So that's with their power drained!

157
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:45,309
I don't even want to think about what
they can do if they got those figs off!

158
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:46,860
I did my work!

159
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,353
Now work over the food!

160
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,160
Oh! What?!

161
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:11,768
Damn, that's a lot of food.

162
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:13,762
Never seen anyone pull that off.

163
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,140
Got a problem?

164
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,740
Yeah, you dumb face.

165
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:24,617
I made one more trip than
you, you know. So what?

166
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:25,860
I was still faster.

167
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,017
No, you weren't.

168
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:29,100
I'm the strongest and the fastest.

169
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:31,197
How do you know how many rocks you hauled?

170
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,337
You can't even count.

171
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:33,360
I can't, too.

172
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,440
My ass, you can.

173
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:39,180
Wait a sec.

174
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:42,461
Weren't they beat up real
bad when they came here?

175
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:44,570
I mean,

176
00:11:44,653 --> 00:11:46,297
it must have been the
food that healed them

177
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:48,757
because it sure as hell
wasn't the slave labor,

178
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:49,670
right?

179
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:52,238
That's not how the human body works.

180
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:56,502
How are we supposed to break their
spirits when they're like this?

181
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,508
Hey, say something to them.

182
00:11:58,740 --> 00:11:59,570
Hmm?

183
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:01,090
Oh.

184
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:08,420
Don't chew too fast. What?

185
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:09,738
Are you there, Mom?

186
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,197
My food!

187
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,320
It's gone!

188
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:37,520
Who did this?

189
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:43,440
My food is all gone!

190
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:45,800
They took every last bite!

191
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:48,220
Somebody here's sleeping on the job!

192
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:50,860
This will not end well.

193
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:58,040
Stop hiding and confess already!

194
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,140
Please, someone help!

195
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:06,600
Oh, man, you were strapped!

196
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,252
You gotta keep crawling!

197
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,400
General Tobon!

198
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:13,460
The perpetrators are
behind bars. Well, good.

199
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:14,940
And the dumplings?

200
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:17,460
They already ate it all.

201
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:20,737
And you two just stood there
and watched while they did it.

202
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:24,817
The thing is, they worked super hard
and got paid the correct amount of food.

203
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:26,547
So what are we going to say?

204
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:27,610
No.

205
00:13:27,693 --> 00:13:31,300
I'm the vice warden here,
and I will stand for you.

206
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:40,000
I can't understand it once
the hippo closes its mouth.

207
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,140
Dobon, sir.

208
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:46,460
I said, bring them here!

209
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:48,280
They'll suffer for this!

210
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:59,480
All right, sir, here
are the culprits. Huh?

211
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:02,440
Teach them a lesson.

212
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:13,550
Let's go!

213
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:17,297
I never thought I see a prisoner
with a belly full of food.

214
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:19,160
I wish that was me!

215
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:24,500
Listen, punks, I'm obviously a big eater,
but you only left me three dumplings.

216
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:25,858
How is that enough?

217
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:29,000
I've got two mouths to feed. Look at me.

218
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:31,760
You think this is a joke?

219
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:33,360
Hold on a sec.

220
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:36,180
I got to digest here.

221
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:39,080
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

222
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:02,180
You prisoners wiped that
stupid grin off your face.

223
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:07,640
My precious Fight!

224
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:12,430
Hey!

225
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:14,937
Wouldn't push my luck if I were you.

226
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:20,377
Maybe you haven't heard, but there's a
rule if you mess with the guards here.

227
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:23,637
Your arms will be cut off
for the first offense.

228
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:26,860
And for the second, your legs.

229
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:33,137
As for the third, you'll
be sentenced to death.

230
00:15:33,220 --> 00:15:35,020
So watch yourself!

231
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:37,840
Got that, newbies?

232
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:41,100
There's no room for defiance against me

233
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:42,990
Listen,

234
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:47,867
you took our powers away with these cuffs
and we still hold that stone for you.

235
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:51,020
You gonna punish us for
working our asses off?

236
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:55,240
Get this through your thick heads, morons!

237
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:04,600
The reason I'm punishing you
is because you ate all my food!

238
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:09,237
All right, fine!

239
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,400
Jaggy.

240
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:17,800
Yibbles!

241
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,440
It's time for you to play!

242
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,920
Poor babies!

243
00:16:29,340 --> 00:16:32,120
It's like a torture shaver inside there!

244
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:33,829
Just wait for the screams!

245
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,560
What the hell happened?

246
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,708
I've never seen the
hippo go down like this.

247
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,360
Vice Warden, are you okay?

248
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:28,700
You're in for it now!

249
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:31,680
You will get the death penalty for sure!

250
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:37,020
It wasn't us. What?

251
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:42,020
If you think that we did
something wrong, proof it.

252
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:49,900
Hell yeah!

253
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:51,720
Tell those jerks!

254
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:53,720
You are my hero!

255
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:15,460
Fresh and ready, get your Sabo today!

256
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,620
You don't want to miss it!

257
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:30,840
Sandoros Special, the best Sabo in town!

258
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:35,520
Do it to me now!

259
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,960
Here you go, ladies.

260
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:43,338
Thanks for waiting.

261
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:04,760
Wow, now that is insanely good.

262
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,980
Any update on Luffy?

263
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:11,097
If he broke out of that labor camp,
we'd probably hear the news, right?

264
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,121
Then again, it's pretty far away.

265
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:17,327
Anyhow, I'm sure he'll be freeing
plenty of time for the raid.

266
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:20,897
I'm glad you made it out
